{
  "_comment": "Hand-verified split points for cached raw TTS takes (VOICE_RAW_DIR/{batch}.wav). The automatic splitter in generate_voice.py mis-aligned the first Hebrew batch by one sentence, so every clip after he.welcome held the wrong words (e.g. he.retry.0 said 'tap the animal to hear again'). Intervals are seconds in the raw take; 'heard' is the transcription of that interval (Gemini listening pass, 2026-11-16), checked against the line text. Applied by scripts/tts/apply_verified_splits.py, which makes no API calls. Game lines (scripts/tts/game-lines.json) are aligned per batch by transcribing every speech segment of the raw take, then each cut clip is transcribed again (Gemini 3.8 Flash listening pass, 2026-11-23) and 'heard' holds that final transcript.",
  "he-df5294e9cc": {
    "he.welcome": {
      "start": 0.21,
      "end": 3.39,
      "heard": "שלום! מי משחקת היום?"
    },
    "he.map.choose": {
      "start": 4.62,
      "end": 10.09,
      "heard": "לאן נלך היום? בואי נבקר בבית השפות!"
